<%#
  A ticket's status, as a badge, in the colour language this console already speaks: red is loud, yellow is
  ours and ticking, green is done, slate is quiet (operations/_severity_badge.html.erb and _status_badge).

  NOTE THE TWO WAITING STATES READ THE OPPOSITE WAY FROM THE CUSTOMER'S SCREEN, and deliberately.
  `waiting_on_customer` pauses the SLA clock, so from this side it is parked: quiet. `waiting_on_lynomia` is
  our own delay with the clock running, so it is the yellow one. On the customer's screen it is the reverse,
  because there "your turn" is the thing they need to see.
%>
<%
  classes = {
    'open' => 'bg-woot-50 text-woot-700 border-woot-300',
    'in_progress' => 'bg-violet-50 text-violet-700 border-violet-200',
    'waiting_on_customer' => 'bg-slate-50 text-slate-700 border-slate-200',
    'waiting_on_lynomia' => 'bg-yellow-50 text-yellow-900 border-yellow-300',
    'resolved' => 'bg-green-50 text-green-800 border-green-200',
    'closed' => 'bg-slate-100 text-slate-600 border-slate-300'
  }
%>
<span class="inline-flex items-center border rounded-md px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium <%= classes.fetch(status, classes['open']) %>">
  <%= status.humanize %>
</span>
